  "created_date": "2026-09-03",
  "claim_scope": "Candidate C9c-3 (both P39 reviews). The second review found the deeper form: a witnessed lane's fragment must EQUAL the one its minted witness carries, and the single registered receipt-backed producer emits controlled and entitlement rows only, so a state placing a reserve, a pending obligation or an open terminal on that lane admits NO accepted certificate however its rows are arranged. The projection derived one anyway; it now refuses with PROJECTION_ROWS_BEYOND_PRODUCER. A consequence stated rather than hidden: under the current registry the whole reserve, external and terminal derivation is unreachable through the entry point, so its contract is exercised through the helpers and is the contract a future producer would have to meet. The same review also showed the source-principal binding CONSTRAINS without DETERMINING: the checker binds a pending row's principal to SOME controlled location, so a cell controlled by two principals still admits two accepted certificates with different allocation roots; the projection refuses those states and the module docstring now says the checker would take either. The primary review's P1: the UNDETERMINED/UNRECONCILABLE separation the previous cut declared was itself false. Unassignable controlled atoms with no pending obligation, and entitlements exceeding custody whenever the outbox happened to be empty, were both returned as ..._AMBIGUOUS although no certificate over those states is acceptable, and the negative-residual code sat after an early return so it could fire only when an outbox entry existed. The residual is now classified before the pending count is consulted; unassignable atoms and an obligation with no controlled location behind it have their own unreconcilable codes; and the suite's standard changed: an UNRECONCILABLE refusal is shown by BUILDING the state-consistent certificate and having the checker refuse it, while the AMBIGUOUS one is shown by exhibiting two certificates the checker accepts. Earlier: Candidate C9c-2 (both P38 reviews): the projection derives the certificate from one exact GlobalEconomicStateV1 and REFUSES with a closed code wherever V1 state does not determine a certificate the checker can accept. The previous cut claimed the projection never yields a certificate failing a row, aggregate or derived-root check: that was FALSE (an OPEN terminal over-claiming its entitlement, two terminals over-claiming together, a claimant with no entitlement, and entitlements exceeding custody all derived certificates the checker must reject) and it was VACUOUS where it was measured, because every row-bearing fixture state has all lanes disabled and the maximum row count across all twenty-nine projected fixture certificates was zero. The family now separates UNDETERMINED (more than one accepted certificate exists: the AMBIGUOUS codes) from UNRECONCILABLE (none exists: TERMINAL_WITHOUT_ENTITLEMENT, TERMINAL_EXCEEDS_ENTITLEMENT, NEGATIVE_RESIDUAL, ROW_TOTAL_OVERFLOW, NO_LANE_FOR_ROWS, MULTIPLE_ENABLED_LANES), every one of the ten codes has a test, and the byte-for-byte witness claim is re-made over a witness whose receipt actually proved a custody row, so it is no longer a statement about an empty witness.",
  "change_kind": "assurance_infrastructure",
  "risk_class": "critical",
